  "raw": {
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a7887a196888d0f01969199a5b65ec5": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor Civil Engineering.  William Jewell College invites applications from outstanding candidates for an Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor in the areas of geotechnical engineering or structural engineering. This is a full-time faculty position beginning in August 2026 with the possibility of starting in January 2026. The successful candidate must be eligible to work in the U.S. prior to the start of the position. Appointment level will be based on an applicant's scholarly and teaching record and practical experience. All Teaching Professor positions, regardless of rank, are non-tenured positions appointed for a three-year limited term period; however, the intent is for this position to be a long-term position. Due to the percentage of effort focused upon instructional duties, all applicants must possess outstanding teaching skills and teach 12 credit hours of regularly scheduled classes per semester. A Ph.D. or M.S. in Civil Engineering or a closely related field is required with the ideal candidate qualified to teach undergraduate courses in structural engineering or geotechnical engineering as well as other introductory civil engineering courses. The successful applicant will have a passion for undergraduate engineering education, assist in program development (course and curriculum development and program assessment), mentor engineering students, especially during their capstone design projects, develop and foster relationships with industry, and recruit and advise students. Preference will be given to applicants with strong leadership skills, the ability to teach a range of undergraduate civil engineering courses, and the desire to integrate fully in a critical thinking college. Qualifications: Ph.D. in Civil Engineering or closely related field is preferred. M.S. in Civil Engineering or closely related field required. Ability to teach across the undergraduate civil engineering curriculum preferred with an emphasis in geotechnical engineering or structural engineering Ability to develop courses, curriculum, and assess and evaluate Professional licensure preferred or ability to obtain within one year. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching 24 contact hours per year Development of curriculum and assessment tools Service to the College and community including academic advising and involvement in College and departmental committees and activities The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by employees in this position. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications of employees assigned to this job. Application Procedures Candidates must submit the following documents in PDF format via email to jobs@william.jewell.edu. Letter of application that addresses the job qualifications including a response to the College Mission, William Jewell Application Resume Statement of teaching experiences and interests, including commentary on teaching at a primarily undergraduate liberal arts college The names, email and contact information for three professional references. Questions can be directed to Maggie Sherer at shererm@william.jewell.edu Applicants, who need accommodation for the application or interview process, please make accommodation requests in advance to the Office of Human Resources. William Jewell College Office of Human Resources 500 College Hill Box 1017 Liberty, MO 6406 (816) 415-5992 Availability Review of applications will begin on 10/15/2025 and continue until position is filled. All Final Candidates will be required to successfully pass a criminal background check prior to beginning employment. Our Mission: We educate our community to ask reflective questions, apply critical thought and act with purpose. We flourish by valuing: Authentic Engagement, Courageous Citizenship, Creative Expression, Inclusive Communities, Innovative Thought, and Spiritual Exploration William Jewell College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0f2672c53025a": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Associate Registrar.  William Jewell College seeks a highly organized and service-oriented Associate Registrar to manage the integrity and efficiency of academic record-keeping, registration, scheduling, and reporting. Reporting to the Registrar, this position is responsible for the daily operations of the Office of the Registrar and ensures that those operations run accurately, on schedule, and in accordance with institutional policy and federal regulation. The Associate Registrar also serves as the office's operational backup to the Registrar for degree audit and graduation functions. Key Responsibilities • Maintain and safeguard official student records, grades, and transcripts; process transcript requests and enrollment and degree verifications. • Manage registration and enrollment operations each term, including registration windows, course permissions, waitlists, add/drop and withdrawal processing, and enrollment status changes. • Build and publish the term course schedule in coordination with division heads and the Registrar; coordinate classroom assignments and resolve conflicts. • Produce and publish the final examination schedule and the term deadline calendar for the Registrar's approval. • Apply academic policy related to registration, grading, enrollment status, and academic standing; process associated forms and workflows. • Prepare enrollment, retention, and completion reports for internal planning, accreditation, and federal and state compliance reporting, including IPEDS and National Student Clearinghouse submissions. • Generate and maintain standard and ad hoc reports from the student information system. • Support the Registrar with athletic eligibility work by compiling roster, enrollment, and grade data each term. • Serve as backup to the Registrar for degree audit review and graduation checks; maintain sufficient cross-training to sustain office operations in the Registrar's absence. • Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) for international students, supporting F-1 student immigration compliance, SEVIS reporting, record maintenance, and student advising related to visa status and regulatory requirements. • Serve as a records and registration resource to students, faculty, advisors, and academic support committees. • Ensure office practice complies with FERPA and maintain records retention and release procedures. • Perform other duties as assigned by the Registrar. Qualifications Required • Bachelor's degree. • Minimum of three years of experience in academic records, registration, or registrar operations. • Working knowledge of FERPA, academic policy, and higher education administrative systems. • Strong attention to detail, time management, and interpersonal skills. Preferred • Master's degree. • Experience with Ellucian Colleague and electronic document workflow systems. • Experience with course scheduling and classroom optimization tools. • Experience with IPEDS and Clearinghouse reporting. • Experience writing queries and building reports in Ellucian Colleague or a comparable SIS (e.g., SQL, Colleague Reporting & Operational Analytics, or Informer) Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a78879ea06420fb01a0a57044984f4a": {
      "title": "Development Services Associate",
      "description": "Development Services Associate.  This part-time position (approximately 20 hours per week) is a key member of the Advancement team and accurately records, codes, and acknowledges all financial contributions. Maintains donor database integrity, tracks restricted funds, and works with the finance team to reconcile donations. Creates and maintains all donor records and provides written correspondence to all College donors on behalf of the President and the Office of Advancement. Duties and Responsibilities Timely entry of daily gifts received (cash, checks, credit cards, stock transfers, and recurring gifts) into the CRM. Prepare and send acknowledgment letters, receipts, and communications to donors and event participants in a timely manner. Creates and distributes daily reports to President, advancement, executive team and Business Office for financial reconciliation. Creates and maintains event records, includes gathering necessary details to set up the accurate record in the database. Manages CRM updates to include new and changed constituent information such as: name, address, telephone number, salutation, codes and attributes. Serve as the primary department contact for demographic updates. Processes matching gift forms for fundraising, make entries into database and send to the appropriate company in a timely fashion. Processes monthly pledge reminders for fundraising, writing off pledges as requested. Strong focus on detail, strict data confidentiality, and basic problem-solving abilities Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Associate’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience Demonstrated proficiency in the use of computer applications including Microsoft Office and the ability to learn the College records system and additional applications. Experience working with donor or CRM databases (Raiser’s Edge NXT preferred) and familiarity with basic financial or expense-reporting processes is a plus. Ability to work collaboratively and interact graciously with donors, alumni, students, faculty, and staff. Strong organizational and time-management skills; ability to manage multiple tasks within a part-time schedule. Working Conditions Normal office environment. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by employees in this position. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications of employees assigned to this job. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a78859e9eb34c5b019ef9e67358555c": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor.  Position title: Financial Aid Counselor Reports to: Director of Financial Aid Department: Student Financial Services FLSA: Exempt The Financial Aid Counselor plays a vital role in supporting students by providing guidance on financial aid options, resources, and policies. This position involves assisting prospective and current students navigating the financial aid process to empower their pursuit of a desired undergraduate or graduate degree or credential. Key Responsibilities Advising Students: Meet with prospective and current students to discuss financial aid options, including grants, loans, and scholarships. Provide personalized guidance based on individual financial situations and deliver clear, concise information regarding financial aid policies, deadlines, and procedures. Respond to inquiries via email, phone, and in-person consultations. Financial Aid Processing: Process financial aid applications, ensuring compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations. Review and analyze student aid applications for accuracy and completeness. Counseling on Financial Literacy: Conduct workshops and individual sessions on financial literacy topics, including budgeting, debt management, and repayment options to empower students in making informed financial decisions. Collaboration and Reporting: Maintain accurate records and documentation of student interactions and financial aid awards. Assist in generating reports for internal analysis and compliance audits. Collaborate with academic program coordinators when necessary/applicable on program-specific data sharing and key performance indicators. Continuous Improvement: Stay current with evolving financial aid regulations and policies and participate in professional development opportunities to enhance knowledge and skills in the financial aid field. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in finance, education, counseling, or a related field. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to advise and advocate for students. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications 2+ years’ experience in financial aid counseling or a related field. Knowledge of federal and state financial aid regulations and processes. Proficiency in financial aid software systems and Microsoft Office Suite. Bilingual or multilingual abilities are a plus. This job description provides an overview of the responsibilities and qualifications for a Financial Aid Counselor, aimed at attracting candidates who are committed to supporting students in their educational pursuits. It does not represent the full scope of daily work or other duties as assigned by the Director of Financial Aid. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a78859fa0f425c801a0fe4dd6cf2d26": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Cross Country, Men's & Women's",
      "description": "Head Coach, Cross Country, Men's & Women's.  William Jewell College, an NCAA Division II institution competing in the Great Lakes Valley Conference (GLVC), invites applications for the position of head men’s and women’s cross country coach. This role is responsible for providing leadership, vision, and direction for all aspects of the cross country programs, including recruiting, coaching, program administration, academic support, and student-athlete development. The head coach will cultivate a competitive, values-driven environment aligned with the College’s mission, institutional priorities, and the Division II “Life in the Balance” philosophy. The head coach will recruit during the 2026-2027 academic year with expectation for full sport sponsorship participation in the fall of 2027. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Program Leadership & Culture · Establish a program identity centered on academic achievement, competitive excellence, and personal growth. · Create a positive, disciplined, and inclusive team culture that emphasizes character, accountability, and high standards. · Plan, implement, and evaluate practice sessions, tactical systems, training cycles, and game-day strategies. · Provide individualized instruction to enhance technical, tactical, and physical development. · Oversee strength training, conditioning, and sport performance in collaboration with campus partners. · Identify, evaluate, recruit, and retain student-athletes who reflect the academic and athletic profile of the College. · Manage all recruiting communication, talent identification, scouting, and on-campus visits in accordance with NCAA and GLVC regulations. · Oversee program budget, team travel, scheduling, equipment inventory, and operational logistics. · Manage assistant coaches, graduate assistants, and student staff (if applicable). · Maintain strong working relationships with athletic training, strength & conditioning, admissions, and academic support services. · Ensure full compliance with NCAA Division II, GLVC, and William Jewell College policies and procedures. · Complete required documentation, reports, and training modules in a timely manner. · Promote a safe, healthy environment for student-athletes. · Represent William Jewell College with professionalism in all internal and external interactions. · Participate in departmental and institutional initiatives, community service, and campus events. · Engage alumni, donors, and the broader community to elevate program visibility and support. Qualifications Required · Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. · Demonstrated coaching experience in cross country (collegiate, club, or professional). · Proven ability to recruit, teach, and develop student-athletes. · Strong understanding of NCAA rules and a commitment to compliance. · Excellent communication, leadership, and organizational skills. Preferred · Master’s degree. · Previous NCAA Division II or collegiate head coaching experience. · Experience in fundraising, alumni engagement, and program-building initiatives. · CPR/First Aid certification. Position Details · Employment Type: Full-time · Compensation: Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications · Benefits: Full William Jewell College benefits package · Work Schedule: Flexible; includes evenings, weekends, and travel as required for training, competition, and recruiting Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a7887a8a03fc2be01a049b0aed233fb": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Business",
      "description": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Business.  Position Overview William Jewell College invites applications for an Instructor or Assistant Professor of Business with emphasis in management, leadership, and business applications of AI. This is a full-time, two-year term position beginning August 2027, with potential for renewal and conversion to tenure-track. Rank and tenure-track eligibility will be determined based on qualifications and experience. At this pivotal moment in business education, we seek a faculty member who can help students navigate the AI-driven transformation of work while grounding them in foundational management and leadership principles. The ideal candidate brings both academic excellence and practical insight into how artificial intelligence is reshaping business strategy, operations, and decision-making. What Makes This Role Distinctive William Jewell's business program combines liberal arts breadth with professional preparation, developing leaders who think critically, communicate effectively, and lead with purpose. This position offers the opportunity to: Shape how a new generation of business leaders understands and leverages AI as a general purpose technology Teach across the business curriculum with flexibility to develop innovative courses at the intersection of management, leadership, entrepreneurship and emerging technologies Engage deeply with undergraduate students through teaching, advising, research mentorship, and co-curricular involvement Contribute to a collaborative department culture focused on teaching excellence and continuous program innovation Qualifications Required: Master's degree (MA or MBA) in Business, Management, or closely related field AND significant professional experience in business management, leadership, or organizational development Demonstrated ability or strong potential to teach effectively across the undergraduate business curriculum, including courses in management, leadership, business law, AI applications in business, and entrepreneurship Commitment to undergraduate teaching excellence and student-centered pedagogy Ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented academic environment Preferred: Ph.D. in Business, Management, Organizational Leadership, or related field Experience integrating AI tools and concepts into business education or professional practice Experience with curriculum development and program assessment Record of scholarly activity, professional consulting, or applied research relevant to business education Primary Responsibilities Teaching (up to 24 contact hours per academic year): Deliver high-quality instruction in business, management, leadership, business law, AI-related business courses, and/or entrepreneurship courses Develop and maintain contemporary, engaging curriculum that prepares students for evolving workplace demands Create effective assessments that measure student learning outcomes and inform continuous improvement Scholarly and Professional Development: Maintain an active program of scholarly activity, which may include traditional academic research, consulting work, applied projects, or other forms of professional engagement Stay current with developments in business practice, management theory, and educational innovation Student Engagement and Mentorship: Provide academic advising to business students Support student research, independent studies, and co-curricular activities Engage with student organizations and professional development initiatives Service: Participate actively in divisional and institutional committees Contribute to college-wide initiatives and community engagement as appropriate Note: The above statements describe the general nature and level of work being performed. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications. Application Process Candidates must submit the following materials in PDF or MS Word format via email to jobs@william.jewell.edu: Letter of application addressing: (a) how your qualifications match the position requirements, (b) your response to William Jewell College's mission, and (c) how you would contribute to inclusivity and diversity on campus Completed William Jewell Application form Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy, including commentary on essential elements of a strong business program at a liberal arts college Evidence of teaching effectiveness (professional teaching evaluations, peer observations, or other documentation, if available) Statement of research and professional development plan Official transcripts for all undergraduate and graduate work (unofficial copies acceptable until finalist stage) Three letters of recommendation will be requested for finalists Applicants who need accommodation for the application or interview process should contact the Office of Human Resources in advance: William Jewell College Office of Human Resources Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a7885ac9efb8722019f4253069e6253": {
      "title": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Instructor or Assistant Professor of Nursing.  Instructor or Assistant Professor of Nursing Division of Behavioral, Natural and Health Sciences FLSA Status: Exempt Summary The Nursing Program in the Division of Behavioral, Natural and Health Sciences at William Jewell College invites applications for a full-time Simulation Coordinator and Instructor/Assistant Professor of Nursing beginning August 2026. This is a full-time, renewable, three-year, non-tenure-track faculty appointment. The successful candidate will provide leadership for the planning, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of simulation-based learning experiences while serving as a member of the undergraduate nursing faculty. This position supports the integration of simulation across the curriculum to promote clinical judgment, critical thinking, communication, and professional practice. In addition to coordinating the Simulation Center, the successful candidate will teach undergraduate nursing courses consistent with departmental needs and individual expertise, including didactic, laboratory, clinical, and simulation instructions. Primary teaching responsibilities are expected to include Adult Health I: Chronic Conditions, with opportunities to teach additional nursing courses as assigned. Faculty rank will be commensurate with academic preparation and teaching experience. Qualifications • Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution • Current unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license or eligibility for Missouri licensure • Teaching experience in prelicensure nursing education or equivalent clinical education experience • Experience in simulation-based nursing education. • Excellent communication, organizational, and collaborative skills. • Experience using learning management systems and instructional technologies. Preferred • Experience teaching medical-surgical nursing and/or undergraduate Adult Health nursing courses. • Experience supporting simulation quality initiatives, accreditation, or endorsement processes. • Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) certification or willingness to obtain certification. Duties and Responsibilities Faculty Responsibilities • Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate nursing courses consistent with departmental needs and then candidate’s expertise, including: Adult Health I: Chronic Conditions Simulation Clinical and laboratory instruction • Teach didactic, laboratory, clinical and simulation courses. • Develop engaging learning experiences that promote clinical reasoning, clinical judgment, and evidence-based practice. • Evaluate student learning and provide timely, constructive feedback. • Serve as an academic advisor, as assigned. Simulation Leadership • Coordinate and oversee simulation activities within the Department of Nursing. • Collaborate with faculty to design, implement and evaluate simulation experiences that support course and program outcomes. • Oversee scheduling, operation, and utilization of the Nursing Simulation Center. • Maintain simulation equipment, technology, supplies, and inventory. • Assist with strategic planning, budgeting, and long-range development of simulation resources. • Recruit, train, and supervise simulation assistants, standardized patients, student workers, and other personnel as appropriate. • Coordinate faculty development related to simulation pedagogy and technologies. • Maintain the department’s INACSL endorsement by overseeing compliance with endorsement standards and leading endorsement renewal activities. • Maintain professional competence through continuing education and engagement in simulation and nursing education best practice. Application Procedure Candidates must submit the following documents through the online application system: • Letter of application addressing qualifications and interest in the position. • Curriculum Vitae. • Statement of teaching philosophy. • Undergraduate and Graduate Transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable until finalists are selected) Please note: Incomplete submissions may not be considered. Availability Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. All final candidates will be required to successfully pass a criminal background check prior to beginning employment. Our Mission: We educate our community to ask reflective questions, apply critical thought and act with purpose. William Jewell College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a78839ea06420ea01a08b7bad7f149b": {
      "title": "Lead Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Lead Groundskeeper.  William Jewell College is seeking a dependable, experienced, and motivated Lead Groundskeeper to help maintain the appearance, safety, and overall condition of our campus grounds. This is a hands-on position with primary responsibility for mowing, turf care, general grounds, walk, and road maintenance, along with seasonal snow and ice removal. The Lead Groundskeeper will help coordinate daily mowing activities, prioritize work based on campus needs and weather conditions, and ensure outdoor spaces are maintained to a high standard. The ideal candidate has professional experience operating commercial lawn and grounds equipment, takes pride in maintaining attractive and well-kept outdoor spaces, and can work independently while providing day-to-day leadership and coordination to grounds activities. Key Responsibilities · Lead and perform mowing and turf maintenance throughout the William Jewell College campus. · Safely operates commercial grounds equipment, including zero-turn and riding mowers, push mowers, string trimmers, edgers, blowers, chainsaws, skid steers, tractors, stump grinder, and related equipment. · Maintain lawns, walkways, landscaped areas, and other outdoor spaces to established campus standards. · Assist with landscape maintenance activities, including planting, mulching, pruning, and weed control. · Inspect equipment before use and perform routine cleaning, lubrication, and basic maintenance. · Identify equipment issues and promptly report necessary repairs or maintenance needs. · Help coordinate mowing schedules and prioritize daily work based on campus activities, events, weather, and seasonal needs. · Assist with grounds setup, cleanup, and preparation for campus events and activities. · Participate in snow and ice removal operations, including operating snow removal equipment, shoveling, and applying ice melt. · Respond to snow and ice removal needs during early mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays when necessary. · Maintain a clean, organized, and safe work environment. · Perform other grounds, facilities, and related duties assigned. Qualifications · Previous professional or commercial mowing and grounds maintenance experience required. · Demonstrated experience operating commercial lawn mowers and other powered lawn and landscape equipment. · Ability to safely operate, inspect, clean, and perform basic maintenance on grounds equipment. · Strong attention to detail and a commitment to maintaining high-quality, well-kept grounds. · Ability to work independently, prioritize tasks, and contribute effectively as part of a team. · Dependable attendance and willingness to respond to operational needs during inclement winter weather. · Valid Missouri Class E (or equivalent) driver’s license and acceptable driving record required. Physical Requirements and Working Conditions This position requires regular outdoor work and the ability to safely operate powered grounds equipment for extended periods. The employee must be able to lift and carry equipment and materials and perform repetitive physical tasks as required. Work is performed in a variety of weather conditions, including extreme heat and cold, rain, snow, and ice. The position may require extended periods of standing, walking, bending, kneeling, lifting, pushing, and pulling. Seasonal snow and ice removal responsibilities may require work outside of normal business hours, including early mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by employees in this position. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications of employees assigned to this job. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a78859fa0f425c801a1226792d37373": {
      "title": "Student Records Specialist",
      "description": "Student Records Specialist.  The Student Records Specialist is responsible for maintaining the accuracy and integrity of student academic records across programs and partners. This role oversees enrollment verification, registration, student status changes, finance hold coordination, transcript evaluation for transfer and graduate students, and related academic operations processes to ensure compliance, consistency, and accurate institutional reporting. Training on transcript evaluation procedures will be provided; no prior evaluation experience is required. Enrollment Verification (EV) • Execute recurring enrollment verification cycles • Confirm academic engagement using LMS and institutional systems • Ensure alignment between student activity and official enrollment records • Maintain compliance with financial aid and institutional requirements Registration & Student Status Management • Register students upon academic and financial clearance • Maintain accurate enrollment records in Colleague • Execute D&C (Defer/Cancel) processes in accordance with institutional policy and timing requirements • Ensure accurate student status updates across systems Finance Hold Coordination • Review students with financial holds impacting registration • Coordinate with Student Financial Services regarding registration readiness • Monitor and maintain hold-related tracking processes Graduation & Academic Progress Tracking • Track students nearing program completion • Maintain internal graduation readiness tracking • Coordinate with institutional registrar for final processing as needed • Monitor academic progress and related status indicators Grade & Academic Records Verification • Support grade verification and tracking processes • Monitor grading timelines and identify missing or overdue grades • Maintain accuracy and integrity of academic records Transcript Evaluation (Transfer & Graduate Students) • Evaluate incoming transfer transcripts to determine applicable credit and course equivalencies • Evaluate graduate-level transcripts for admission and program-fit requirements • Apply institutional articulation guidelines and program-specific transfer credit policies • Document evaluation decisions accurately in Colleague and related systems • Coordinate with academic departments on non-standard or ambiguous credit evaluations • Training on transcript evaluation procedures, tools, and institutional policy will be provided; no prior evaluation experience is required Student Records & Systems Management • Maintain accurate student data in Colleague and related systems • Identify and resolve inconsistencies in academic records • Support institutional reporting and audit readiness • Maintain structured operational tracking systems Key Characteristics for Success • High attention to detail and accuracy • Strong organizational and process management skills • Ability to manage recurring, deadline-driven workflows • Comfort working independently in structured operational environments • Experience with student information systems (Colleague preferred) • Willingness to learn transcript and credit evaluation standards (training provided) Role Boundaries This role is not responsible for: • Admissions communication or applicant follow-up • High-volume student inbox management • General intake or frontline issue resolution This role focuses on records integrity, compliance, transcript/credit evaluation, and structured academic operations Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a78879e9d4aea52019d928a3ce77b9a": {
      "title": "Success Coach",
      "description": "Success Coach.  Job Title: Success Coach Reports To: Dean of Student Success, Academic Affairs FLSA Status: Non-Exempt, Full-Time Position Summary William Jewell College seeks a student-centered, relational, and data-informed professional to serve as a Success Coach. Reporting to the Dean of Student Success, the Success Coach provides proactive, holistic support to undergraduate students to promote persistence, academic achievement, and timely degree completion. Grounded in Jewell’s commitment to rigorous liberal arts education and individualized attention, the Success Coach partners with students to help them navigate academic, social, and personal transitions. This role works collaboratively across academic and student affairs to ensure students are connected to the resources, relationships, and strategies necessary for success. Primary Responsibilities Student Coaching & Support Provide individualized success coaching Develop proactive outreach strategies for students identified through early alerts, academic performance indicators, or retention risk factors. Assist students in goal setting, time management, academic planning, and skill development. Support students in navigating transitions (first-year, transfer, academic probation, major exploration, return from leave). Retention & Intervention Monitor academic progress using institutional data systems and early alert platforms. Coordinate intervention plans for students experiencing academic or personal challenges. Facilitate success workshops or small group sessions on topics such as study strategies, academic resilience, and campus resource navigation. Collaboration & Referral Serve as a liaison between students and faculty, academic advisors, athletics, residence life, counseling services, and other campus offices. Participate in cross-functional retention and student support initiatives. Contribute to case management discussions as appropriate. Data & Assessment Maintain accurate documentation of student interactions. Analyze student success trends to inform proactive outreach strategies. Assist in assessing retention initiatives and student success programming. Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree (Master’s preferred) in Higher Education, Counseling, Student Affairs, or related field. Experience working with college students in an advising, coaching, or student support capacity. Demonstrated ability to build trusting relationships with diverse student populations. Strong organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills. Ability to use data systems and student information platforms effectively. Preferred Experience with early alert systems, case management software, or CRM platforms. Understanding of liberal arts education and small-college environments. Training in coaching methodologies, motivational interviewing, or student development theory. Core Competencies Relational leadership and empathy Proactive, student-centered mindset Collaborative approach across campus divisions Data-informed decision-making Working Conditions This position requires regular in-person engagement with students and collaboration across campus. Occasional evening hours may be required to support programming and student outreach. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c66c5073a7016cb555a9e46cdf&id=8a78879ea15447f701a1839a9a5d1057": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Civil Engineering.  William Jewell College invites applications for a Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor in the areas of geotechnical engineering or water resource engineering. This is a full-time faculty position beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate must be eligible to work in the U.S. prior to the start of the position. Appointment level will be based on an applicant's scholarly and teaching record and practical experience. A Ph.D. or M.S. in Civil Engineering or a closely related field is required with the ideal candidate qualified to teach undergraduate courses in geotechnical engineering as well as other introductory and design courses within civil engineering. The successful applicant will have a passion for undergraduate engineering education, assist in program development (course and curriculum development and program assessment), mentor engineering students, especially during their capstone design projects, develop and foster relationships with industry, and recruit and advise students. Qualifications: · Ph.D. in Civil Engineering or closely related field is preferred. M.S. in Civil Engineering or closely related field required. · Ability to teach across the undergraduate civil engineering curriculum preferred with an emphasis in geotechnical engineering or water resource engineering · Ability to develop courses, curriculum, and assess and evaluate · Professional licensure preferred or ability to obtain within one year. Duties and Responsibilities: · Teaching 24 contact hours per year · Development of curriculum and assessment tools · Service to the College and community including academic advising and involvement in College and departmental committees and activities · Engagement of undergraduate students in research and/or project based learning The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by employees in this position. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities, and qualifications of employees assigned to this job. Application Procedures Candidates must submit the following documents in PDF format with their application. · Letter of application that addresses the job qualifications including a response to the College Mission · Resume · Statement of teaching experiences and interests, including commentary on teaching at a primarily undergraduate liberal arts college · The names, email and contact information for three professional references. Applicants, who need accommodation for the application or interview process, please make accommodation requests in advance to the Office of Human Resources. William Jewell College Office of Human Resources 500 College Hill Box 1017 Liberty, MO 6406 hr@william.jewell.edu Availability Review of applications will begin on 12/15/2026 and continue until position is filled. All Final Candidates will be required to successfully pass a criminal background check prior to beginning employment. Our Mission: We educate our community to ask reflective questions, apply critical thought and act with purpose. We flourish by valuing: Authentic Engagement, Courageous Citizenship, Creative Expression, Inclusive Communities, Innovative Thought, and Spiritual Exploration William Jewell College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
